<title>GREECE: IFC TO ISSUE 27.5 BLN DRACHMA FRN DUE 02 -LEADS.</title>
<headline>IFC TO ISSUE 27.5 BLN DRACHMA FRN DUE 02 -LEADS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Finance Corporation (IFC) will issue a 27.5 billion drachma floating rate note due 2002 at three-month Athibor minus 75 basis points, joint lead managers Barclays, Athens (books) and Alpha Credit Bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>Maturity date is August 27, 2002 and coupon payments are quarterly commencing November 27, it said.</p>
<p>The issue was approved by the Athens stock exchange authorities today.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
